        {
          "text": "HUANG Yü-chi 黃虞稷 (T. 俞邰 and 楮園), 1629–1691, scholar and bibliophile, was a native of Shang-yüan (Nanking). His family came originally from Chin-chiang, Fukien, but moved to Kiangsu when his father, Huang Chü-chung 黃居中 (T. 明立, H. 海鶴, chü-jên of 1585), became proctor of the Imperial Academy at Nanking.",
          "source": "eccp-3640032",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "黃虞稷，字俞邰，上元人，本籍晉江。",
          "source": "qsg-volume-484",
          "kind": "biographical-opening",
          "status": "proposed"
        }
